gnosis-fix",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hans/swe/incident-diagnosis-fix.md",fullPath:"/zh-hans/swe/incident-diagnosis-fix",subtoc:"basic",order:22,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=事故时如何有效诊断问题与修正错误?",summary:"本文介绍事故发生时，工程团队如何用有结构的方式排查问题并修正错误。内容整理 Google SRE 专书中的 effective troubleshooting 方法，包含分流与检查、诊断问题、测试假设，以及先止损再追根因的处理原则。"},{title:"事故時如何有效診斷問題與修正錯誤?",date:"2026-07-29",lastmod:"2026-07-29",toc:"devops",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"incident-diagnosis-fix",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hant/swe/incident-diagnosis-fix.md",fullPath:"/zh-hant/swe/incident-diagnosis-fix",subtoc:"basic",order:22,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=事故時如何有效診斷問題與修正錯誤?",summary:"本文介紹事故發生時，工程團隊如何用有架構的方式排查問題並修正錯誤。內容整理 Google SRE 專書中的 effective troubleshooting 方法，包含分流與檢視、診斷問題、測試假設，以及先止損再追根因的處理原則。"},{title:"Choosing the Right Frontend Rendering Strategy",date:"2026-07-23",lastmod:"2026-07-23",toc:"frontend",lang:"en",fileName:"frontend-rendering-strategies",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/frontend-rendering-strategies.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/frontend-rendering-strategies",subtoc:"frontend-performance",order:11,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=Choosing the Right Frontend Rendering Strategy",summary:"This article explains the most common frontend rendering strategies, from client-side rendering and traditional server-side rendering to modern SSR with hydration and streaming. It compares their trade-offs in loading performance, SEO, and interactivity so you can choose the right approach for your project."},{title:"前端渲染模式的选择",date:"2026-07-23",lastmod:"2026-07-23",toc:"frontend",lang:"zh-hans",fileName:"frontend-rendering-strategies",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hans/swe/frontend-rendering-strategies.md",fullPath:"/zh-hans/swe/frontend-rendering-strategies",subtoc:"frontend-performance",order:11,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=前端渲染模式的选择",summary:"本文介绍前端常见的渲染模式，从客户端渲染、传统服务器端渲染，到搭配注水与流式传输的现代 SSR。通过比较各模式在加载性能、SEO 与交互体验上的取舍，帮助前端工程师根据项目需求选择合适的渲染策略。"},{title:"前端渲染模式的選擇",date:"2026-07-23",lastmod:"2026-07-23",toc:"frontend",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"frontend-rendering-strategies",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hant/swe/frontend-rendering-strategies.md",fullPath:"/zh-hant/swe/frontend-rendering-strategies",subtoc:"frontend-performance",order:11,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=前端渲染模式的選擇",summary:"本文介紹前端常見的渲染模式，從客戶端渲染、傳統伺服器端渲染，到搭配注水與串流的現代 SSR。透過比較各模式在載入效能、SEO 與互動體驗上的取捨，協助前端工程師依專案需求選擇合適的渲染策略。"},{title:"Before Building Claude Code, Boris Cherny Lived in Nara Making Miso",date:"2026-07-16",lastmod:"2026-07-16",toc:"career-talk",lang:"en",fileName:"boris-cherny-before-claude-code",filePath:"src/pages/en/career/boris-cherny-before-claude-code.md",fullPath:"/en/career/boris-cherny-before-claude-code",subtoc:"career-thinking",order:16,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=Before Building Claude Code, Boris Cherny Lived in Nara Making Miso",summary:"Before joining Anthropic, Claude Code creator Boris Cherny lived in Nara while working fully remotely as a principal engineer at Instagram. By returning to hands-on coding, delegating leadership, and embracing asynchronous communication, he expanded his impact far from Silicon Valley and learned from miso making to build Claude Code with a longer time horizon."},{title:"开发出 Claude Code 前，Boris Cherny 曾在奈良过着酿味噌的生活",date:"2026-07-16",lastmod:"2026-07-16",toc:"career-talk",lang:"zh-hans",fileName:"boris-cherny-before-claude-code",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hans/career/boris-cherny-before-claude-code.md",fullPath:"/zh-hans/career/boris-cherny-before-claude-code",subtoc:"career-thinking",order:16,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=开发出 Claude Code 前，Boris Cherny 曾在奈良过着酿味噌的生活",summary:"Claude Code 创造者 Boris Cherny 在加入 Anthropic 前，曾住在奈良，一边酿味噌，一边以全远程方式担任 Instagram 首席工程师。他通过重新投入写程序、授权他人与异步沟通，在远离硅谷的时区持续扩大影响力，也从酿味噌中学会以更长远的眼光打造 Claude Code。"},{title:"開發出 Claude Code 前，Boris Cherny 曾在奈良過著釀味噌的生活",date:"2026-07-16",lastmod:"2026-07-16",toc:"career-talk",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"boris-cherny-before-claude-code",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hant/career/boris-cherny-before-claude-code.md",fullPath:"/zh-hant/career/boris-cherny-before-claude-code",subtoc:"career-thinking",order:16,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=開發出 Claude Code 前，Boris Cherny 曾在奈良過著釀味噌的生活",summary:"Claude Code 創造者 Boris Cherny 在加入 Anthropic 前，曾住在奈良，一邊釀味噌，一邊以全遠端方式擔任 Instagram 首席工程師。他透過重新投入寫程式、授權他人與非同步溝通，在遠離矽谷的時區持續擴大影響力，也從釀味噌學會用更長期的眼光打造 Claude Code。"},{title:"What Is an SLO? Why SLOs Matter for Software Teams",date:"2026-02-01",lastmod:"2026-07-14",toc:"devops",lang:"en",fileName:"slo-what-is-slo-and-how-to-set-slo",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/slo-what-is-slo-and-how-to-set-slo.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/slo-what-is-slo-and-how-to-set-slo",subtoc:"basic",order:51,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=What Is an SLO? Why SLOs Matter for Software Teams",summary:"Learn what SLOs, or service-level objectives, are and why they matter in software reliability engineering. This article explains the differences between SLI, SLO, and SLA, and why teams should use percentiles such as P50, P95, and P99 instead of relying only on averages when measuring reliability."},{title:"SLO 是什么? 为什么 SLO 对软件团队很重要? ",date:"2026-02-01",lastmod:"2026-07-14",toc:"devops",lang:"zh-hans",fileName:"slo-what-is-slo-and-how-to-set-slo",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hans/swe/slo-what-is-slo-and-how-to-set-slo.md",fullPath:"/zh-hans/swe/slo-what-is-slo-and-how-to-set-slo",subtoc:"basic",order:51,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=SLO 是什么? 为什么 SLO 对软件团队很重要?",summary:"深入了解 SLO（服务水准目标）的定义，以及它在软件可靠性工程中的关键角色。本文说明 SLI、SLO 与 SLA 三者的差异，也补充为什么衡量可靠性时不该只看平均数，而应使用 P50、P95、P99 等百分位点来观察真实用户体验。"},{title:"SLO 是什麼? 為什麼 SLO 對軟體團隊很重要? ",date:"2026-02-01",lastmod:"2026-07-14",toc:"devops",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"slo-what-is-slo-and-how-to-set-slo",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hant/swe/slo-what-is-slo-and-how-to-set-slo.md",fullPath:"/zh-hant/swe/slo-what-is-slo-and-how-to-set-slo",subtoc:"basic",order:51,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=SLO%20%E6%98%AF%E4%BB%80%E9%BA%BC%3F%20%E5%A6%82%E4%BD%95%E7%82%BA%E5%9C%98%E9%9A%8A%E8%A8%AD%E5%AE%9A%20SLO%3F",summary:"深入了解 SLO（服務水準目標）的定義，以及它在軟體可靠性工程中的關鍵角色。本文說明 SLI、SLO 與 SLA 三者的差異，也補充為什麼衡量可靠性時不該只看平均數，而應使用 P50、P95、P99 等百分位點來觀察真實使用者體驗。"},{title:"What Is Latency, and Why Does It Matter?",date:"2026-07-09",lastmod:"2026-07-09",toc:"fullstack-case",lang:"en",fileName:"latency-explained",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/latency-explained.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/latency-explained",subtoc:"backend",order:5,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=What Is Latency, and Why Does It Matter?",summary:"Latency is the waiting time between an event happening and its result becoming visible, and it is one of the most important non-functional requirements in system design. This article explains why low latency matters through user experience, real-time systems, software efficiency, and the tradeoff between latency and throughput."},{title:"延迟 (latency) 是什么? 为什么很重要?",date:"2026-07-09",lastmod:"2026-07-09",toc:"fullstack-case",lang:"zh-hans",fileName:"latency-explained",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hans/swe/latency-explained.md",fullPath:"/zh-hans/swe/latency-explained",subtoc:"backend",order:5,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=延迟 (latency) 是什么? 为什么很重要?",summary:"延迟是从某件事发生到结果被看见之间的等待时间，也是系统设计中常见的重要非功能需求。本文从用户体验、实时系统、效率优化与吞吐量取舍等角度，说明为什么低延迟对软件系统很重要。"},{title:"延遲 (latency) 是什麼? 為什麼很重要?",date:"2026-07-09",lastmod:"2026-07-09",toc:"fullstack-case",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"latency-explained",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hant/swe/latency-explained.md",fullPath:"/zh-hant/swe/latency-explained",subtoc:"backend",order:5,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=延遲 (latency) 是什麼? 為什麼很重要?",summary:"延遲是從某件事發生到結果被看見之間的等待時間，也是系統設計中常見的重要非功能需求。本文從使用者體驗、即時系統、效率優化與吞吐量取捨等角度，說明為什麼低延遲對軟體系統很重要。"},{title:"Different Career Paths for Engineers in the AI Era",date:"2026-07-02",lastmod:"2026-07-02",toc:"career-talk",lang:"en",fileName:"engineer-career-paths-ai-era",filePath:"src/pages/en/career/engineer-career-paths-ai-era.md",fullPath:"/en/career/engineer-career-paths-ai-era",subtoc:"career-advancement",order:11,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=Different Career Paths for Engineers in the AI Era",summary:"Boris Cherny, the creator of Claude Code, observed that as AI reshapes how teams work, roles are starting to blur beyond the old engineering, product, and design boundaries. The five archetypes he describes can help teams understand what kind of people they need at each product stage, but individual engineers should be careful not to let those labels limit their growth."},{title:"AI 时代工程师职业发展的不同路线",date:"2026-07-02",lastmod:"2026-07-02",toc:"career-talk",lang:"zh-hans",fileName:"engineer-career-paths-ai-era",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hans/career/engineer-career-paths-ai-era.md",fullPath:"/zh-hans/career/engineer-career-paths-ai-era",subtoc:"career-advancement",order:11,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=AI 时代工程师职业发展的不同路线",summary:"Claude Code 作者 Boris Cherny 观察到，AI 时代的团队角色正在从传统工程、产品、设计分工，转向原型探索者、建造者、整理者、成长者与维护者等不同典型。这种分类有助于团队理解不同阶段需要什么人才，但个人不该因此被定型，而应随着产品与团队演进持续调整自己的角色。"},{title:"AI 時代工程師職涯發展的不同路線",date:"2026-07-02",lastmod:"2026-07-02",toc:"career-talk",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"engineer-career-paths-ai-era",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hant/career/engineer-career-paths-ai-era.md",fullPath:"/zh-hant/career/engineer-career-paths-ai-era",subtoc:"career-advancement",order:11,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=AI 時代工程師職涯發展的不同路線",summary:"Claude Code 作者 Boris Cherny 觀察到，AI 時代的團隊角色正在從傳統工程、產品、設計分工，轉向原型探索者、建造者、整理者、成長者與維護者等不同典型。這種分類有助於團隊理解不同階段需要什麼人才，但個人不該因此被定型，而應隨著產品與團隊演進持續調整自己的角色。"},{title:"DDIA Chapter 5 Guide — Encoding and Evolution, Part 1",date:"2026-06-28",lastmod:"2026-06-28",toc:"system-design-tutorial",lang:"en",fileName:"ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-1",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-1.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-1",subtoc:"intro",order:15,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=DDIA Chapter 5 Guide — Encoding and Evolution, Part 1",summary:"This guide covers the first half of Chapter 5 of Designing Data-Intensive Applications, explaining why data must be encoded once it leaves process memory and how formats such as JSON, XML, and Protocol Buffers differ. It also introduces forward and backward compatibility, and why schema evolution matters for long-lived systems."},{title:"DDIA Chapter 5 Guide — Encoding and Evolution, Part 2",date:"2026-06-28",lastmod:"2026-06-28",toc:"system-design-tutorial",lang:"en",fileName:"ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-2",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-2.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-2",subtoc:"intro",order:16,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=DDIA Chapter 5 Guide — Encoding and Evolution, Part 2",summary:"This guide covers the second half of Chapter 5 of Designing Data-Intensive Applications, explaining how data format evolution affects databases, client-server communication, RPC, and asynchronous messaging systems. It focuses on why forward and backward compatibility matter during deployment, migration, and event-driven data flows."},{title:"DDIA 导读 CH5 — 编码与演化（上）",date:"2026-06-28",lastmod:"2026-06-28",toc:"system-design-tutorial",lang:"zh-hans",fileName:"ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-1",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hans/swe/ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-1.md",fullPath:"/zh-hans/swe/ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-1",subtoc:"intro",order:15,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=DDIA 导读 CH5 — 编码与演化（上）",summary:"本文导读《Designing Data-Intensive Applications》第五章前半段，说明为什么数据离开内存后需要被编码，以及 JSON、XML、Protocol Buffers 等格式各自的取舍。文章也梳理 schema 演化时的向前兼容与向后兼容问题，帮助读者理解数据格式如何影响系统长期演进。"},{title:"DDIA 导读 CH5 — 编码与演化（下）",date:"2026-06-28",lastmod:"2026-06-28",toc:"system-design-tutorial",lang:"zh-hans",fileName:"ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-2",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hans/swe/ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-2.md",fullPath:"/zh-hans/swe/ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-2",subtoc:"intro",order:16,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=DDIA 导读 CH5 — 编码与演化（下）",summary:"本文导读《Designing Data-Intensive Applications》第五章后半段，说明数据格式演化如何影响数据库、客户端与服务器端、RPC，以及异步消息系统。文章梳理向前兼容与向后兼容在部署、数据迁移与事件驱动架构中的实务意义。"},{title:"DDIA 導讀 CH5 — 編碼與演化 (上)",date:"2026-06-28",lastmod:"2026-06-28",toc:"system-design-tutorial",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-1",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hant/swe/ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-1.md",fullPath:"/zh-hant/swe/ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-1",subtoc:"intro",order:15,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=DDIA 導讀 CH5 — 編碼與演化 (上)",summary:"本文導讀《Designing Data-Intensive Applications》第五章前半段，說明為什麼資料離開記憶體後需要被編碼，以及 JSON、XML、Protocol Buffers 等格式各自的取捨。文章也整理 schema 演化時的向前相容與向後相容問題，幫助讀者理解資料格式如何影響系統長期演進。"},{title:"DDIA 導讀 CH5 — 編碼與演化 (下)",date:"2026-06-28",lastmod:"2026-06-28",toc:"system-design-tutorial",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-2",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hant/swe/ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-2.md",fullPath:"/zh-hant/swe/ddia-ch5-encoding-evolution-part-2",subtoc:"intro",order:16,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=DDIA 導讀 CH5 — 編碼與演化 (下)",summary:"本文導讀《Designing Data-Intensive Applications》第五章後半段，說明資料格式演化如何影響資料庫、客戶端與伺服器端、RPC，以及非同步訊息系統。文章整理向前相容與向後相容在部署、資料遷移與事件驅動架構中的實務意義。"},{title:"How Can Teams Handle Incidents Effectively?",date:"2026-06-18",lastmod:"2026-06-18",toc:"devops",lang:"en",fileName:"incident-response-team",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/incident-response-team.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/incident-response-team",subtoc:"basic",order:21,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=How Can Teams Handle Incidents Effectively?",summary:"Incident response cannot start only after an incident happens. This article explains the foundations engineering teams should build in advance, including reducing alert noise, maintaining runbooks, deploying in small batches, using feature flags, clarifying roles, and creating enough psychological safety for people to stay calm under pressure."},{title:"如何确保团队能有效面对与处理事故?",date:"2026-06-18",lastmod:"2026-06-18",toc:"devops",lang:"zh-hans",fileName:"incident-response-team",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hans/swe/incident-response-team.md",fullPath:"/zh-hans/swe/incident-response-team",subtoc:"basic",order:21,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=如何确保团队能有效面对与处理事故?",summary:"事故处理不能等到事故发生才开始准备。本文整理工程团队在事故前应建立的基础，包括降低告警噪音、建立 runbook、小批次部署、功能旗标、明确分工，以及通过心理安全让成员能冷静处理问题。"},{title:"如何確保團隊能有效面對與處理事故?",date:"2026-06-18",lastmod:"2026-06-18",toc:"devops",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"incident-response-team",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hant/swe/incident-response-team.md",fullPath:"/zh-hant/swe/incident-response-team",subtoc:"basic",order:21,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=如何確保團隊能有效面對與處理事故?",summary:"事故處理不能等到事故發生才開始準備。本文整理工程團隊在事故前應建立的基礎，包含降低警報噪音、建立 runbook、小批次部署、功能旗標、明確分工，以及透過心理安全讓成員能冷靜處理問題。"},{title:"How to Use AI Without Losing Your Technical Judgment",date:"2026-06-12",lastmod:"2026-06-12",toc:"ai-engineering",lang:"en",fileName:"avoid-ai-eroding-technical-judgment",filePath:"src/pages/en/ai/avoid-ai-eroding-technical-judgment.md",fullPath:"/en/ai/avoid-ai-eroding-technical-judgment",subtoc:"ai-with-engineer",order:11,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=How to Use AI Without Losing Your Technical Judgment",summary:"AI agents can make engineering teams faster, but over-reliance can lead to cognitive surrender: accepting AI output without understanding or verification. This article explains the risk through research and real-world examples, then offers practical mechanisms such as pre-commit quizzes, human sign-off, and accountable review practices."},{title:"如何避免用 AI 用到失去技术判断力?",date:"2026-06-12",lastmod:"2026-06-12",toc:"ai-engineering",lang:"zh-hans",fileName:"avoid-ai-eroding-technical-judgment",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hans/ai/avoid-ai-eroding-technical-judgment.md",fullPath:"/zh-hans/ai/avoid-ai-eroding-technical-judgment",subtoc:"ai-with-engineer",order:11,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=如何避免用 AI 用到失去技术判断力?",summary:"AI 代理能提升工程效率，但如果工程师不再检验输出，就可能陷入认知投降，逐渐失去技术判断力。本文整理研究与实际案例，并提出提交前自我测验、人工签署与负责任审查等做法，帮助团队在使用 AI 时保留理解与判断。"},{title:"如何避免用 AI 用到失去技術判斷力?",date:"2026-06-12",lastmod:"2026-06-12",toc:"ai-engineering",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"avoid-ai-eroding-technical-judgment",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hant/ai/avoid-ai-eroding-technical-judgment.md",fullPath:"/zh-hant/ai/avoid-ai-eroding-technical-judgment",subtoc:"ai-with-engineer",order:11,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=如何避免用 AI 用到失去技術判斷力?",summary:"AI 代理能提升工程效率，但若工程師不再檢驗輸出，就可能陷入認知投降，逐漸失去技術判斷力。本文整理研究與實務案例，並提出提交前自我測驗、人工簽署與負責任審查等做法，幫助團隊在使用 AI 時保留理解與判斷。"},{title:"The Tradeoffs Between Stateful and Stateless Software Design",date:"2026-06-08",lastmod:"2026-06-08",toc:"system-design-tutorial",lang:"en",fileName:"stateful-stateless-tradeoffs",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/stateful-stateless-tradeoffs.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/stateful-stateless-tradeoffs",subtoc:"basic",order:8,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=The Tradeoffs Between Stateful and Stateless Software Design",summary:"Stateful and stateless design is not about which one is universally better. It is about where state should live, who should manage it, and how that choice affects scalability, latency, performance, and failure modes."},{title:"软件设计中的有状态 (stateful) 与无状态 (stateless) 的取舍",date:"2026-06-08",lastmod:"2026-06-08",toc:"system-design-tutorial",lang:"zh-hans",fileName:"stateful-stateless-tradeoffs",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hans/swe/stateful-stateless-tradeoffs.md",fullPath:"/zh-hans/swe/stateful-stateless-tradeoffs",subtoc:"basic",order:8,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=软件设计中的有状态 (stateful) 与无状态 (stateless) 的取舍",summary:"有状态与无状态不是单纯谁比较好，而是状态该放在哪里、由谁负责管理的取舍。本文从认证机制、HTTP 与 WebSocket 等案例，说明两种设计在扩展性、性能、延迟与故障风险上的差异。"},{title:"軟體設計中的有狀態 (stateful) 與無狀態 (stateless) 的取捨",date:"2026-06-08",lastmod:"2026-06-08",toc:"system-d