,href:"/en/swe/array-flatten"},{title:"How to find the average of an array in JavaScript?",date:"2023-02-11",lastmod:"2024-03-06",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"find-average-in-an-array",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/find-average-in-an-array.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/find-average-in-an-array",subtoc:"array",order:3,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=How to find the average of an array in JavaScript?",summary:"Learn how to find the average of an array in JavaScript efficiently. This blog post provides two solutions: a traditional for loop solution and a functional programming reduce solution. Understand the logic behind each solution and enhance your JavaScript skills for interviews and coding challenges.",href:"/en/swe/find-average-in-an-array"},{title:"How to remove duplicates from an array?",date:"2022-12-21",lastmod:"2024-03-06",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"remove-duplicates",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/remove-duplicates.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/remove-duplicates",subtoc:"array",order:4,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=How to remove duplicates from an array?",summary:"Learn multiple solutions to remove duplicates from an array efficiently in JavaScript. This tutorial covers four methods: using Set, filter with indexOf, nested for loop, and utilizing Object or Map. Enhance your JavaScript skills and be well-prepared for array manipulation challenges in interviews and real-world scenarios.",href:"/en/swe/remove-duplicates"}]},{title:"Function",links:[{title:"What Is an Arrow Function in JavaScript? How Is It Different From a Regular Function?",date:"2022-10-27",lastmod:"2022-10-27",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"what-is-arrow-function",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/what-is-arrow-function.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/what-is-arrow-function",subtoc:"function",order:0,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=What Is an Arrow Function in JavaScript? How Is It Different From a Regular Function?",summary:"Arrow function is a function expression introduced in ES6. Some features of an arrow function are different from a regular function expression. It is a common question in JavaScript interviews, so make sure you know the difference",href:"/en/swe/what-is-arrow-function"},{title:"What is an IIFE (Immediately Invoked Function Expression) in JavaScript? What are the Pros and Cons?",date:"2023-02-13",lastmod:"2023-02-13",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"what-is-iife",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/what-is-iife.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/what-is-iife",subtoc:"function",order:1,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=What is an IIFE (Immediately Invoked Function Expression) in JavaScript? What are the Pros and Cons?",summary:"This article explains the concept of Immediately Invoked Function Expression (IIFE) in JavaScript, its syntax, and its benefits, such as creating a local scope, avoiding naming conflicts, enabling modular programming, and improving code execution efficiency. It also discusses the disadvantages of IIFEs, such as difficulty in maintenance, bad reusability, and increased code complexity. The article provides an example of a classic interview question related to setTimeout, scope, and IIFE and offers solutions to the problem.",href:"/en/swe/what-is-iife"},{title:"What Is a Higher-Order Function in JavaScript?",date:"2023-02-15",lastmod:"2023-02-15",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"what-is-hof",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/what-is-hof.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/what-is-hof",subtoc:"function",order:2,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=What Is a Higher-Order Function in JavaScript?",summary:"The article explains the concept of higher order functions, which is the ability of a function to receive another function as a parameter or return a function as its result. This technique is important in functional programming and can help improve code modularity, reusability, and maintenance. The article also provides examples of higher order functions, such as callback function wrapping, abstraction of operations, and function composition.",href:"/en/swe/what-is-hof"}]},{title:"Objects & Prototypes",links:[{title:"The most common JavaScript prototype interview questions and answers (prototype, prototypal inheritance, prototype chain)",date:"2023-02-02",lastmod:"2023-02-02",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"most-common-js-prototype-questions",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/most-common-js-prototype-questions.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/most-common-js-prototype-questions",subtoc:"object",order:0,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=The most common JavaScript prototype interview questions and answers (prototype, prototypal inheritance, prototype chain)",summary:"In this article, we will introduce the most common JavaScript prototype interview questions and answers. Including what is prototype, what is the difference between __proto__ and [[Prototype]], what is the difference between __proto__ and prototype, what is the prototype chain, what is prototypal inheritance, etc.",href:"/en/swe/most-common-js-prototype-questions"},{title:'What Is "this" in JavaScript?',date:"2023-02-13",lastmod:"2023-02-13",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"what-is-this",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/what-is-this.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/what-is-this",subtoc:"object",order:1,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=What Is this in JavaScript?",summary:"Learn about the concept of this in JavaScript, including how it refers to objects and how to use the apply(), call(), and bind() methods to control its behavior. Get a better understanding of how this works in different contexts and scenarios.",href:"/en/swe/what-is-this"},{title:"Explaining the Concept of a Class in ES6 and the Distinction Between a Function Constructor",date:"2023-02-09",lastmod:"2023-02-09",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"what-is-class",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/what-is-class.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/what-is-class",subtoc:"object",order:2,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=Explaining the Concept of a Class in ES6 and the Distinction Between a Function Constructor",summary:"This article explains the class concept in JavaScript and the difference between ES6 class and ES5 function constructor. The class was introduced in ES6 as syntactic sugar, which simulates class behavior through prototypal inheritance. The article covers various aspects of class including inheritance, static methods, and private fields. It is an essential read for front-end developers and anyone preparing for JavaScript interviews.",href:"/en/swe/what-is-class"},{title:"When Is the Difference Between Shallow and Deep Copy in JavaScript?",date:"2024-11-01",lastmod:"2024-11-01",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"shallow-copy-and-deep-copy",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/shallow-copy-and-deep-copy.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/shallow-copy-and-deep-copy",subtoc:"object",order:4,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=When Is the Difference Between Shallow and Deep Copy in JavaScript?",summary:"When working with JavaScript, developers often encounter two distinct ways of copying non-primitive data types such as objects and arrays: shallow copy and deep copy.",href:"/en/swe/shallow-copy-and-deep-copy"},{title:"Why structuredClone is the Best Choice for Deep Copying in JavaScript?",date:"2024-11-05",lastmod:"2024-11-05",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"structureClone",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/structureClone.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/structureClone",subtoc:"object",order:5,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=Why structuredClone is the Best Choice for Deep Copying in JavaScript?",summary:"this piece explains why structureClone is becoming the go-to solution for deep copying in JavaScript, offering better performance and compatibility than traditional methods.",href:"/en/swe/structureClone"}]},{title:"Event Loop、Promise、Async/Await",links:[{title:"What Is JavaScript Promise? And How To Use It?",date:"2023-02-14",lastmod:"2023-02-14",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"what-is-promise",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/what-is-promise.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/what-is-promise",subtoc:"event-loop",order:0,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=What Is JavaScript Promise? And How To Use It?",summary:"Promise is a new feature in ES6, and it is used to optimize the previous callback function. This interview in-depth discussion will discuss what promise is, why we need Promise, and extend to async/await related questions.",href:"/en/swe/what-is-promise"},{title:"What Is an Event Loop in JavaScript?",date:"2023-02-14",lastmod:"2023-02-14",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"what-is-event-loop",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/what-is-event-loop.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/what-is-event-loop",subtoc:"event-loop",order:1,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=What Is an Event Loop in JavaScript?",summary:"Understanding the event loop is a crucial concept for JavaScript developers. The event loop consists of a call stack, task queue, and heap. Asynchronous tasks are divided into macro and micro tasks, with different execution orders. The event loop executes one macro task at a time and completes all micro tasks before executing the next macro task. Common macro tasks include setTimeout, setInterval, I/O, events, and postMessage. Micro tasks include Promise.then, MutationObserver, and process.nextTick. requestAnimationFrame and requestIdleCallback have different execution timings.",href:"/en/swe/what-is-event-loop"},{title:"The Most Common JavaScript Event Loop Interview Questions",date:"2023-01-22",lastmod:"2023-01-25",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"js-event-loop-questions",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/js-event-loop-questions.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/js-event-loop-questions",subtoc:"event-loop",order:2,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=The Most Common JavaScript Event Loop Interview Questions",summary:"The event loop is a common question in interviews. In addition to knowing the concept, You also need to know how it works in code. Here we have listed common JavaScript event loop code interpretation questions",href:"/en/swe/js-event-loop-questions"},{title:"What is Promise.race? How to implement it?",date:"2022-10-06",lastmod:"2022-10-06",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"javascript-whiteboard-promise-race",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/javascript-whiteboard-promise-race.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/javascript-whiteboard-promise-race",subtoc:"event-loop",order:3,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=What is Promise.race? How to implement it?",summary:"What is Promise.race()? It receives an `Iterable` (e.g. Array, Map, Set) with multiple promises inside it, and returns whichever is first fulfilled or first rejected",href:"/en/swe/javascript-whiteboard-promise-race"},{title:"What is Promise.all? How to implement it?",date:"2022-10-06",lastmod:"2022-10-06",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"javascript-whiteboard-promise-all",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/javascript-whiteboard-promise-all.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/javascript-whiteboard-promise-all",subtoc:"event-loop",order:4,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=What is Promise.all? How to implement it?",summary:"As a front-end engineer, you might use Promise.all() in daily development very often, but do you know how to implement this method? This is a very common question in interviews. If you still do not know how to do it, let us explain it step by step through this article.",href:"/en/swe/javascript-whiteboard-promise-all"},{title:"What are async/await in JavaScript and how do they differ from promises?",date:"2024-11-06",lastmod:"2024-11-06",toc:"javascript",lang:"en",fileName:"async-await",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/async-await.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/async-await",subtoc:"event-loop",order:10,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=What are async/await in JavaScript and how do they differ from promises?",summary:"async/await is JavaScript's elegant solution to handling asynchronous operations. While it's built on top of Promises, it offers a cleaner, more intuitive way to write code. async declares functions that return Promises, while await lets you extract their values. Compared to the lengthy .then and .catch chains in Promises, async/await makes asynchronous code read like synchronous code, with more straightforward error handling and better readability.",href:"/en/swe/async-await"}]}],"zh-hant-react":[{title:"目錄",links:[{title:"React 面試題詳解 - 導覽",date:"2023-08-26",lastmod:"2024-01-27",toc:"react",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"react",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hant/swe/react.md",fullPath:"/zh-hant/swe/react",subtoc:"table-of-content",order:0,images:"https://explainthis-image.octave.vip/8cb7a5ceb26146748127623dfdc5671f.png",summary:"本系列彙整了常見的 React 面試題，包含 React 基礎、React Hooks、React 進階",href:"/zh-hant/swe/react"}]},{title:"React 基礎",links:[{title:"什麼是純函式 (pure function)? 為什麼 React 的函式元件需要是純函式?",date:"2022-02-04",lastmod:"2022-02-04",toc:"react",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"react-pure-function",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hant/swe/react-pure-function.md",fullPath:"/zh-hant/swe/react-pure-function",subtoc:"basic",order:0,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=什麼是純函式 (pure function)? 為什麼 React 的函式元件需要是純函式?",summary:"在 Hook 出現後，React 的函式元件 (Function Component) 逐漸成為主流。關於函式元件，最常見的問題之一，便是「為什麼 React 的函式元件需要是純函式 (pure function)?」。本篇將以第一人稱的方式，擬答這個問題。",href:"/zh-hant/swe/react-pure-function"},{title:"什麼是 JSX? 為什麼要用 JSX?",date:"2022-10-24",lastmod:"2022-10-24",toc:"react",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"what-is-jsx",filePath:"src/pages/zh-hant/swe/what-is-jsx.md",fullPath:"/zh-hant/swe/what-is-jsx",subtoc:"basic",order:1,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=什麼是 JSX? 為什麼要用 JSX?",summary:"JSX 在語法上看起來與 HTML 相近，但它其實是 JavaScript 的語法擴展。它的特點是，UI 與 JavaScript 邏輯的相融 - 組合成元件。雖然 React 官方沒有強制要求使用 JSX 來開發 React，但使用上來說，大多數人覺得對開發體驗比較好，它也可以讓 React 顯示一些錯誤和提示訊息。",href:"/zh-hant/swe/what-is-jsx"},{title:"請解釋 React 生命週期？",date:"2022-11-16",lastmod:"2022-11-16",toc:"react",lang:"zh-hant",fileName:"react-lifecycle",filePath:"