 of the ExplainThis website redesign case study. Discover why stability, support, and cost-effectiveness outweigh the allure of new, cutting-edge technologies. Understand the importance of focusing on customer needs and strategic progression in technology choices. Find out why choosing boring technologies can lead to more reliable, maintainable, and cost-effective websites.",href:"/en/swe/boring-technology"},{title:"Writing Maintainable Code — Boolean Condition Best Practices",date:"2023-10-21",lastmod:"2025-09-13",toc:"swe-read",lang:"en",fileName:"boolean-readability",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/boolean-readability.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/boolean-readability",subtoc:"senior",order:4,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=Writing Maintainable Code — Boolean Condition Best Practices",summary:"This article summarizes insights from former Google senior engineer Max Kanat-Alexander's article 'Improve Readability With Positive Booleans'.",href:"/en/swe/boolean-readability"},{title:"How to Write Good Documentation as an Software Engineer",date:"2025-06-11",lastmod:"2025-06-11",toc:"swe-read",lang:"en",fileName:"swe-how-to-write-doc",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/swe-how-to-write-doc.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/swe-how-to-write-doc",subtoc:"senior",order:10,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=How to Write Good Documentation as an Software Engineer",summary:"Software engineers need strong documentation skills to advance their careers. This guide explores the tangible benefits of good documentation, from improving your thinking clarity to expanding your influence, and provides practical advice on identifying your audience, focusing on key messages, and adapting your writing style to different document types.",href:"/en/swe/swe-how-to-write-doc"},{title:"How to Take Better Technical Notes",date:"2026-03-25",lastmod:"2026-03-25",toc:"swe-read",lang:"en",fileName:"how-to-write-good-technical-notes",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/how-to-write-good-technical-notes.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/how-to-write-good-technical-notes",subtoc:"senior",order:11,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=How to Take Better Technical Notes",summary:"This article explains why technical notes should be more than storage and retrieval for software engineers. It argues that effective note-taking is a thinking process, then shows how to apply the Cornell Method in practice by writing questions first, updating understanding as you learn, and summarizing your own insights.",href:"/en/swe/how-to-write-good-technical-notes"}]},{title:"Others",links:[{title:"Software Engineer Acronyms You'll Hear at Work (Understand RFC, SEV, SLA, and More)",date:"2025-09-30",lastmod:"2025-09-30",toc:"swe-read",lang:"en",fileName:"software-engineering-acronyms",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/software-engineering-acronyms.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/software-engineering-acronyms",subtoc:"else",order:1,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=Software Engineer Acronyms You'll Hear at Work (Understand RFC, SEV, SLA, and More)",summary:"This guide gathers the acronyms software engineers rely on at work so you can stay confident when someone drops another three-letter code.",href:"/en/swe/software-engineering-acronyms"},{title:"How Should Senior Engineers Oversee Code Reviews?",date:"2026-01-22",lastmod:"2026-01-22",toc:"swe-read",lang:"en",fileName:"senior-engineer-code-review-gatekeeper",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/senior-engineer-code-review-gatekeeper.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/senior-engineer-code-review-gatekeeper",subtoc:"else",order:18,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=How Should Senior Engineers Oversee Code Reviews?",summary:"Exploring how senior engineers can elevate code review practices at the team level, focusing on systemic quality improvements, knowledge transfer, and fostering a healthy team culture. Addresses common pitfalls like lenient reviews, emotional attacks, and unconstructive feedback.",href:"/en/swe/senior-engineer-code-review-gatekeeper"},{title:"