s/en/swe/javascript-cost.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/javascript-cost",subtoc:"frontend",order:1,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=The Cost of JavaScript",summary:"Explore the impact of JavaScript on web performance in this insightful article. Learn about optimizing JavaScript to enhance user experience, including techniques like code splitting, server-side rendering, island architecture, and zero JavaScript. Discover how these strategies can improve load times, especially for mid-to-low-end devices and slow network connections.",href:"/en/swe/javascript-cost"}]},{title:"Backend Case",links:[{title:"How Does Netflix Migrate High-Traffic Systems Without Downtime?",date:"2023-12-29",lastmod:"2023-12-29",toc:"fullstack-case",lang:"en",fileName:"system-design-netflix-migration",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/system-design-netflix-migration.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/system-design-netflix-migration",subtoc:"backend",order:0,images:"https://www.explainthis.io/api/og?title=How Does Netflix Migrate High-Traffic Systems Without Downtime?",summary:"In system design interviews, a common follow-up question is 'How would you migrate the system?' Netflix's official tech blog provides a real-world case study in 'Migrating Critical Traffic At Scale with No Downtime — Part 1'.",href:"/en/swe/system-design-netflix-migration"},{title:"How the Threads Team Built the Fastest App to Reach 100 Million Users",date:"2023-12-20",lastmod:"2023-12-20",toc:"fullstack-case",lang:"en",fileName:"system-design-threads",filePath:"src/pages/en/swe/system-design-threads.md",fullPath:"/en/swe/system-design-threads",subtoc:"backend",order:2,images:"https://explainthis-image.octave.vip/48332408f972471a88d896ad9a889b9e.png",summary:"What engineering decisions enabled Instagram's team to build Threads - the app that broke ChatGPT's record for fastest user growth - in just 5 months? Let's examine their approach to team structure, technology choices, and quality practices.",href:"/en/swe/system-design-threads"